    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1147">

                <pb facs="1060" n="802" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg802"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the</hi>
                    
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                    
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-09-02T14:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 2, 1915, 2 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 9.55 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>56. Department’s circular telegram of August 30. Sweden embargoed export arms and
                    ammunition chiefly in order to conserve them for home use but also on account of
                    attitude of British Government <pb facs="1061" n="803" xml:id="pg803"/> in
                    retaliating on Swedish commerce in cases export from Sweden to Germany. Sale
                    would have been purely negligible quantity.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
